WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.212 --> 00:00:24.972
Brooklyn stared at her phone in shock. Who had sent her this mean text? Girls can't coach. Especially oafs like u.

2
00:00:24.974 --> 00:00:30.711
A player who hated her, obviously. She glanced uneasily around the gym.

3
00:00:30.712 --> 00:00:41.801
It was empty, except for two janitors, who were sweeping, and Marv, who was locking up the equipment closet.

4
00:00:41.802 --> 00:00:49.697
Brooklyn pulled back her shoulders. An elementary school teacher had once taught Brooklyn's class how to handle bullies.

5
00:00:49.698 --> 00:00:54.530
One thing Brooklyn remembered was to never let bullies bother you.

6
00:00:54.531 --> 00:00:59.193
And if they did bother you, you were supposed to talk to an adult about it.

7
00:00:59.194 --> 00:01:07.097
"Take that!" Brooklyn pressed Delete on her phone. She instantly felt better.

8
00:01:07.098 --> 00:01:16.831
But at school on Monday, Brooklyn found a note folded up inside her locker: You're no coach!

9
00:01:16.832 --> 00:01:27.070
On Tuesday there was another note in her lunch bag: We need a real coach. Not you.

10
00:01:27.071 --> 00:01:35.421
On Wednesday she found one in her gym bag: Leave the Whales.

11
00:01:35.422 --> 00:01:43.318
On Thursday a note lay inside her history book: Quit or the team will lose.

12
00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:53.330
Brooklyn kept the messages to herself. But on Friday she pulled Jacey aside before math class.

13
00:01:53.331 --> 00:02:01.480
She showed her the latest note, found in her backpack that morning: Oafs don't coach.

14
00:02:01.481 --> 00:02:05.794
Jacey's eyes widened. "That's so mean."

15
00:02:05.795 --> 00:02:12.546
"It's not the first message I've gotten this week." Brooklyn told her friend about the other messages.

16
00:02:12.547 --> 00:02:15.868
"Have you told anyone?" Jacey asked.

17
00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.666
Brooklyn shook her head.

18
00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:25.044
"The final game is coming up, so I didn't want to get anyone in trouble. Do you think Dirk wrote these notes?"

19
00:02:25.045 --> 00:02:30.049
Jacey shrugged. "I know Dirk was mad about being benched."

20
00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:39.013
"That was his fault, not mine," Brooklyn said as the bell rang. "We'll talk more at practice," she said quickly.

21
00:02:39.014 --> 00:02:42.925
But Brooklyn didn't get a chance to talk to Jacey at practice.

22
00:02:42.926 --> 00:02:50.767
Instead she spent almost the entire session walking around school searching for Dirk.

23
00:02:50.768 --> 00:02:57.346
Someone said they saw him in the office, so she checked there. No Dirk.

24
00:02:57.347 --> 00:03:02.421
Someone else claimed he was in the library. No Dirk.

25
00:03:02.422 --> 00:03:06.747
This was their last practice before the play-off game on Saturday.

26
00:03:06.748 --> 00:03:16.418
While Marv led the team through the loop play, Brooklyn used the phone in the gym office.

27
00:03:16.419 --> 00:03:23.552
She called Dirk's cell phone and his home, but no one answered either number.

28
00:03:23.553 --> 00:03:31.647
When Brooklyn went to tell Marv the news, she heard Jacey laughing out in the hall at the water fountain.

29
00:03:31.648 --> 00:03:34.929
"She wants to be a professional coach!"

30
00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:38.566
"Really?" Stuart laughed.

31
00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:42.387
"Can you coach if you don't even play?" Aaron asked.

32
00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:48.315
"Brooklyn wants to," said Jacey. "It's her big dream."

33
00:03:48.316 --> 00:03:58.533
Brooklyn hurried away before they spotted her. "I can't believe Jacey told them about my dream of coaching," she thought.

34
00:03:58.534 --> 00:04:06.048
Tears stung her eyes. It was the truth, but the way Jacey had said it made Brooklyn feel silly.

35
00:04:06.049 --> 00:04:12.461
Were Aaron and Stuart laughing at her? She blinked quickly to keep her tears from spilling.

36
00:04:12.462 --> 00:04:25.356
Outside the gym Brooklyn took a few deep breaths. She had to calm down.

37
00:04:25.357 --> 00:04:31.767
The team had had a great season. And if things went well, they could be league champions.

38
00:04:31.768 --> 00:04:41.407
She squared her shoulders and stepped onto the basketball court next to Marv. "What's next, Coach?"

39
00:04:41.408 --> 00:04:46.002
After practice Brooklyn put away the equipment.

40
00:04:46.003 --> 00:04:51.239
Marv looked at her. "You were awfully quiet today," he said.

41
00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:56.662
"I was worried about . . . um, the final game. And Dirk."

42
00:04:56.663 --> 00:05:02.226
"We'll be fine," Marv said grimly. "With or without Dirk."

43
00:05:02.227 --> 00:05:10.142
When Brooklyn reached her house thirty minutes later, she was surprised to see Dirk sitting on her front steps holding a basketball.

44
00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:16.467
"Where were you?" Brooklyn demanded. "Today's final practice was super important."

45
00:05:16.468 --> 00:05:21.638
"I went to talk to Coach Teagan," Dirk said. "About the team.

46
00:05:21.639 --> 00:05:25.313
And after talking to you, I'm going to talk to Marv."

47
00:05:25.314 --> 00:05:33.627
Dirk took a big breath. "I didn't like you giving us plays, but you do seem to know your stuff.

48
00:05:33.628 --> 00:05:38.442
I know I haven't been a team player, and I'm sorry."

49
00:05:38.443 --> 00:05:44.765
Brooklyn was proud to hear Dirk say she knew her stuff with basketball. "It's okay," she said.

50
00:05:44.766 --> 00:05:49.953
"Thanks. And don't worry. I didn't let those notes bother me."

51
00:05:49.954 --> 00:05:53.415
Dirk frowned, confused. "What notes?"

52
00:05:53.416 --> 00:05:59.930
Brooklyn studied his face. "You didn't leave mean notes for me? Or text me?"

53
00:05:59.931 --> 00:06:05.842
Dirk shook his head. "That's creepy, Brooklyn. I'd never do something like that."

54
00:06:05.843 --> 00:06:09.585
"If it wasn't you . . . ," Brooklyn began.

55
00:06:09.586 --> 00:06:12.770
"What do the notes say?" Dirk asked.

56
00:06:12.771 --> 00:06:19.999
"Uh . . . never mind," she said quickly. She was still worried about upsetting the team before the final game.

57
00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:26.840
"Anyway, Marv said you'll have to sit out for the first quarter of tomorrow's game because you missed practice.

58
00:06:26.841 --> 00:06:30.837
But the Whales still need you for the other three quarters."

59
00:06:30.838 --> 00:06:40.005
Dirk stood up straighter, but he didn't respond to Brooklyn. He took a one-handed shot over Brooklyn's head.

60
00:06:40.006 --> 00:06:44.581
The ball swooshed through the basket over the garage.

61
00:06:44.582 --> 00:06:53.305
"Nice shot," Brooklyn said. Dirk had a lousy attitude sometimes, but he was definitely their team's best player.

62
00:06:53.306 --> 00:06:56.242
Dirk scooped up the ball and looked at Brooklyn.

63
00:06:56.243 --> 00:07:07.538
"Coach said I'd better step up for the team and stop being Dirk the Jerk. Catch!" he said, suddenly tossing the ball at her.

64
00:07:07.539 --> 00:07:13.133
"Hey!" Brooklyn laughed as the ball bounced past her.

65
00:07:13.134 --> 00:07:16.493
"Is that revenge for my giving you a black eye?"

66
00:07:16.494 --> 00:07:18.630
"Yep."

67
00:07:18.631 --> 00:07:31.771
Brooklyn got the ball and started dribbling in the driveway. She and Dirk practiced some passes and quick shots into the basket.

68
00:07:31.772 --> 00:07:36.191
Then Brooklyn stopped playing. "Don't you love basketball?"

69
00:07:36.192 --> 00:07:45.451
"Coach Teagan asked me the same question." Dirk swallowed. "Playing basketball makes me happier than anything else in the world."

70
00:07:45.452 --> 00:07:53.091
"I guess I'm thinking like a coach." Brooklyn grinned. "I know some Whales don't like that I'm helping Marv, right?"

71
00:07:53.092 --> 00:07:54.592
Dirk nodded.

72
00:07:54.593 --> 00:08:02.763
"No matter what, I'm not going to quit. There's just one more game left, and I'm sure I can help our team win the championship.

73
00:08:02.764 --> 00:08:06.684
Besides, the end-of-the-season party is at my house!"

74
00:08:06.685 --> 00:08:12.501
Brooklyn tossed Dirk the basketball, which he caught.

75
00:08:12.502 --> 00:08:17.403
"So?" Dirk spun the ball on one finger.

76
00:08:17.404 --> 00:08:23.857
"You can help the team too. I've been working on a move that I call a Michael Jordan Jedi Jump."

77
00:08:23.858 --> 00:08:28.486
Brooklyn jumped from side to side in front of Dirk.

78
00:08:28.487 --> 00:08:37.313
Dirk grinned. "Jordan will always be the king of the court. If Jordan were in Star Wars, he could beat Darth Vader."

79
00:08:37.314 --> 00:08:43.233
"Yep, and with this move, you might wipe that Terrier giant off the court tomorrow.

80
00:08:43.234 --> 00:08:47.551
Instead of Dirk the Jerk, you'll be Dirk the Jedi!"

81
00:08:47.552 --> 00:08:59.860
Brooklyn grabbed the ball from Dirk's hands and whipped it around her body. "So, do you want to give it a try?"
